   Since \( A \triangle B = (A \setminus B) \cup (B \setminus A) \subseteq A \), it follows that both \( A \setminus B \) and \( B \setminus A \) must be subsets of \( A \).  
   \[
   A \setminus B \subseteq A \quad \text{and} \quad B \setminus A \subseteq A.
   \]

