- For \(x = 0\), both functions evaluate to \(0\), so \(x = 0\) is a root.
- The function \(\sin x\) is bounded by \(-1 \leq \sin x \leq 1\). Therefore, the equation \(\sin x = \frac{x}{20}\) can only have additional roots if \(\sin x\) is within the range \([-1, 1]\). This implies \(\sin x \leq 1\), so \(\frac{x}{20} \leq 1\), which implies \(x \leq 20\).

