The coefficient of intrinsic momentum (or induced momentum) of a material \( \kappa_1 \) is defined as the ratio of the induced momentum to the kinetic energy of the material. When the material is observed in a medium with a different inductance \( \kappa' \), the coefficient of intrinsic momentum is modified due to the interaction due to the magnetic field. The effect is given by the following equation:

