","(a) The force on the proton is given by the relationship \( F = \mu I \rho \), where \( \mu \) is the mass, \( I \) is the force, and \( \rho \) is the force per mass.  
The force on the projectile is given by:  
\[
F = \mu \rho = \rho \mu
\]  
Substituting the values:  
\[
F = 500 \, \text{N/C} \times 1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg} = 835 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{N}
\]  
The acceleration \( v \) is given by:  
\[
v = \frac{I}{\mu} = \frac{835 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} \approx 999 \, \text{m/s}^2
\]  
Thus, the acceleration of the projectile is \(\boxed{999 \, \text{m/s}^2}\).  

(b) The acceleration \( v \) is constant, so we can use the equation of motion:  
\[
v = v_0 + v \tau
\]  
where \( v \) is the final velocity, \( v_0 \) is the initial velocity, \( v \) is the acceleration, and \( \tau \) is the time.  
Given \( v_0 = 0 \, \text{m/s} \), \( v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s} \), and \( v = 999 \, \text{m/s}^2} \), we solve for \( \tau \):  
\[
35,000 \, \text{m/s} = 0 \, \text{m/s} + 999 \, \text{m/s}^2 \times \tau
\]  
\[
\tau = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s}}{999 \, \text{m/s}^2} \approx 34.33 \, \text{s}
\]  
Thus, it takes the pellet is approximately \(\boxed{34.33 \, \text{s}}\) to reach a speed of \( 35,000 \, \text{m/s} \).",ground_truth_similarity,"# Task Description
