 T = Torque of the force
m = Mass of the pulley
g = Gravity of the spring
r = Radius of the pulley

The tangential acceleration (v) of point P is given by the formula:

v = v / r

Where:

v = tangential acceleration
v = velocity of the particle
r = Radius of the pulley

The tangential acceleration of point P is given as 2 m/s². The relationship between the net force (F) and tangential acceleration (v) is:

F = (m * v) / r

Plugging in the values:

F = (1 kg * 2 m/s²) / 0.5 m
F = 4 N

